quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  67,13,"(Whether) you speak secretly or loudly, indeed, He is All-Knowing of what is (hidden) in the breasts."
  67,14,"Does He Who created (everything) not know? He is the All-Attentive, the All-Aware."
  67,15,"He is the One Who made the earth subservient to you. So, travel in its (different) routes and eat from His provision. And towards Him is the Resurrection."
  67,16,Do you feel secure that the One in Heaven will not cause the earth to swallow you up when it quakes violently?
  67,17,Or do you feel secure that the One in Heaven will not unleash a storm of stones upon you? You shall soon (come to) know how (severe) My Warning is!
  67,18,And surely those before them had (also) denied; then how (terrible) was My Rebuttal!
  67,19,"Have they not seen the birds above them expanding and contracting their wings? Nothing can hold them (from falling) except (the command of) the Most-Compassionate (Lord). Indeed, He is All-Seeing of everything."
  67,20,Or who is it that could be a force for you to help you besides the Most-Compassionate (Lord)? The disbelievers are only (lost) in delusion.
  67,21,"Or who is it that could provide for you if He withholds His sustenance? Instead, they persist in defiance and aversion."
  67,22,Is the one who crawls upon his face better guided or the one who walks upright on a straight path?
  67,23,"Say: ‘He is the One Who created you and endowed you with ears, eyes and hearts. (Yet) you hardly give any thanks.’"
  67,24,"Say: ‘He is the One Who scattered you throughout the earth, and to Him you shall be gathered.’"
  67,25,They say: ‘When will this promise come to pass if you are truthful?’
  67,26,Say: ‘(Its) knowledge is only with Allah. And I am just a manifest Warner.’
